       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Your confirming it doesn't change the problem. Sertraline 1000 mg is five times the maximum daily dose of 200 mg, and a dose that high could seriously harm the patient. You've also said you're not a clinician, so you can't be the prescriber who authorizes it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n\n- **If the dose was a typo**, give me the intended dose, such as 100 mg, and I'll enter it. A prescriber should still confirm it.\n- **If a prescriber really intends 1000 mg**, they should contact the pharmacy and enter or discuss the order directly. The pharmacist will probably want to review the dose first.\n- **If you're unsure where the order came from**, check with the medicine service team before doing anything else."
